            <ArticleTitle>Iatrogenic acute coronary dissection during coronary angioplasty for in-stent restenosis: role of intravascular ultrasound in diagnosis and treatment.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>E1-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report on a case of coronary dissection resulting from a guidewire passing out of a stent during in-stent restenosis (ISR) treatment and a guidewire successfully negotiated into true lumen and an implanted stent under intravascular ultrasound guidance, resulting in optimal coronary blood flow.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
